  "chapter": 497,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 61 Chapter 497\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 6565, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the agriculture and markets law, in relation to\n        examining the need for standards for the designation of  therapy\n        dogs and the definition and identification of therapy dogs\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  Therapy  dogs  play  an  increasingly important role in supporting the\nill, elderly, and those individuals  suffering  from  diseases  such  as\nanxiety  and post-traumatic stress disorder. This bill would require the\nDepartment of Agriculture and Markets  (DAM)  to  conduct  a  study  and\nsubmit  a  report  examining  the need for standards on the designating,\nlicensing, and training of therapy dogs. It would also update the  defi-\nnition  of  \"therapy dog\" to clarify that they do not qualify as service\ndogs and would authorize municipalities to grant a license tag for these\nanimals.\n \n  I fully support this bill's laudable goal, but as originally  drafted,\nit raises administrative and technical concerns that would impede effec-\ntive  implementation.  To  address  these  concerns,  the  Executive has\nsecured an agreement with the Legislature to  pass  legislation  in  the\nupcoming session to require DAM to convene State and industry experts to\nexamine  the  need  for  statewide  standards  for therapy dogs. On that\nbasis, I am signing this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                      (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2017
 },
